  "authoringNote": "C09 R03 regression. Each current usable order is checked on its own and elements are never combined across orders, so A's signature cannot satisfy B: R03.element_missing (element.signature) names B, missing, authorization coordinator, needs_information. B states the beneficiary name, so the beneficiary element is satisfied by that alternative and no identifier is required or invented. A's identifier and signature beside B's nulls are a stated value beside null, not a disagreement, so no orders_disagree holds; all other stated values are equal. R03 is missing with that one condition; the parent set is empty (C07: a missing-element condition names its order while the parent set stays empty). No \"verified signature\" label exists. Citations, non-null only: R03 nine for A and six for B (fifteen); R02 nine (B has no identifier); R04 nine (both orders final, same date and identifier, after the encounter, so R04 passes); R05 eight (each receipt links its own order and follows the span end 2026-09-02T12:00Z); R01 nine (both codes). R06 five, R07 one. State needs_information.",
